<div class="wrap">
<section class="hero">
  <div class="eyebrow">JusPrin · printer setup by chat · UI walkthrough</div>
  <h1>Printer Setup Walkthrough</h1>
  <p>The printer setup conversation, walked live three times in the shell harness with the real model, from “+ Add printer” through adding, changing the nozzle, connecting, and back to Home. Twelve findings, ranked by how much they hurt a first-time user, each with a screenshot and a pointer to the code that draws it.</p>
  <div class="meta"><span><b>Branch</b> jusprin-newui, working tree of 2026-09-23</span><span><b>Build</b> RelWithDebInfo 13:48, harness <code>--manual-live-agent</code></span><span><b>Model</b> the configured OpenAI provider</span><span><b>Theme</b> light and dark</span></div>
  <div class="summary">
    <div class="tile"><div class="k">Findings</div><div class="v">12 <small>4 high · 4 medium · 4 low</small></div></div>
    <div class="tile"><div class="k">Live runs</div><div class="v">3 <small>same input, three different after-add scripts</small></div></div>
    <div class="tile"><div class="k">Left unverified</div><div class="v">3 <small>wizard fallback, Bambu path, resize scroll</small></div></div>
  </div>
</section>

<h2>About the screenshots</h2>
<div class="note">
  <p>Every state below was seen in the live app first. The desktop screenshot tool did not write its files to disk, so the images here are the same built Agent and Home pages rendered again in a scripted browser with the host state replayed (the same text, cards, and card states, at the app window's 1200 px width). Layout, copy, and controls are the app's own; only the printer thumbnails and the exact line wrapping can differ slightly from the WebKit view inside the app.</p>
  <p>Two things in the live run that cannot be reproduced this way are described in words: the window title turning to “*Untitled” after an add, and the native file picker behind the Photo button.</p>
</div>

<h2>Findings</h2>
